== D5: what the Lambda-force remark adds (not in the pre-declared menu; reported for completeness, not counted in the census) ==
  [OK] the mass on which the Hubble-horizon Lambda-acceleration c H exerts a force equal to the whole vacuum tension F_Lambda is m = 3*c**3/(2*G*H) = 3 M_H, which is M_e again: a0 = F_max/m = c H F_max/F_Lambda; a second description of the same restatement
  [OK] and the mass on which cH exerts exactly F_max is M_H/2 (q = 1 by definition: the acceleration is cH itself)

